   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the social services law, in relation to the licensing or\nregistration of certain programs operated by a public school district or by a\nprivate school or academy",
    "basePrintNo": "S6415",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6415-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 8,
       "fullName": "John E. Brooks",
       "imgName": "923_John_Brooks.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 1101,
       "sessionMemberId": 1803,
       "sessionYear": 2021,
       "shortName": "BROOKS"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §390, Soc Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Social Services Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6415\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the social services law, in relation to the licensing or\nregistration of certain programs operated by a public school district or\nby a private school or academy\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill exempts all kindergarten, pre-kindergarten, or nursery schools\noperated by a school district, private school or academy which is\nauthorized to teach other compulsory grades levels, from licensing\nrequirements as a day care under the Office of Children and Family\nServices, irrespective of whether the program is operated at the same\nlocation that the compulsory grades are taught at.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends clause (D) of subparagraph (ii) of paragraph (a) of\nsubdivision 1 of section 390 of the social services law to expand the\nexception to the term \"daycare\" to exempt all pre-kindergarten, kinder-\ngarten and nursery schools that are operated by a school district,\nprivate school or academy otherwise licensed by the State Education\nDepartment, irrespective of whether the pre-kindergarten, kindergarten\nor nursery school is operated in the same building that other grades are\ntaught at.\n\nSection two provides that this act shall take effect September 1, 2021.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder current law, a school otherwise licensed by SED, that operates a\nkindergarten, pre-kindergarten or nursery school at a location that\ndiffers from the location that compulsory grades are offered, must\nobtain licensure from the Office of Children and Family Services.  This\nmandate adds additional burdens to school districts as they develop\nplans to offer prekindergarten classes to their communities and deal\nwith lack of space caused by the social distancing requirements of the\npandemic. This bill will streamline the process for licensure for pre-\nkindergarten programs, by keeping all licensure requirements within the\npurview of the State Education Department.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis bill shall take effect September 1, 2021.\n",
